[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m Next, we factorize \(9!\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m \[ 9! = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 5 \times 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m We need to find the sum of the positive divisors of \(362880\) that have a units digit of 1. A number with a units digit of 1 must be congruent to 1 modulo 10. Therefore, we need to find the divisors of \(362880\) that are congruent to 1 modulo 10.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m The divisors of \(362880\) can be written as \(2^a \times 3^b \times 5^c \times 7^d\) where \(0 \leq a \leq 7\), \(0 \leq b \leq 4\), \(0 \leq c \leq 1\), and \(0 \leq d \leq 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=320149)[0m We need \(N \equiv 1 \mod 10\). This implies \(N \equiv 1 \mod 2\) and \(N \equiv 1 \mod 5\). Since \(N\) must be odd, \(a = 0\). Thus, \(N = 3^b \times 7^d\).
